Pacman - a tribute to the 1980 maze game, in JavaScript
=======================================================

A personal, non-commercial tribute to Namco's 1980 arcade game.
Pac-Man is a trademark of Bandai Namco; this program is not connected
with them.

!Pacman, in the Diversions directory on the hard disc, is a maze game
after that arcade classic. You steer Pac-Man round a maze, eating the
dots, while a ghost chases you. The whole program is in the
application directory, as JavaScript you can read in !JsEdit and
change; it is built on GameLib, the library of game parts in
!Boot.Resources (see the GameLib guide).

This is an early version. It has the maze, the dots and energizers,
and all four ghosts, who take turns to hunt you and to head for their
corners. Energizers turn the ghosts blue, flashing at the end, and
you can eat them for 200 to 1600 points. There is fruit to eat, and
a level ends when the last dot goes; the next one begins with the
dots back. Lives, with a life taken and an extra one given at 10000, and
GAME OVER, are in. Sounds, a settings page and high scores are still
to come, and parts 5 to 7 below will be written as they arrive.

